## Goal

Record the CAP Dreams idea in the existing long-horizon architecture owner without changing the current product roadmap or production runtime.

## What this adds

- defines CAP Dreams as a future shadow-first, read-only/offline improvement layer;
- maps verified CAP execution history into conceptual `DreamEpisodeV1` / `ReplayWorldV1` / `DreamPolicyV1` / `DreamEvaluationV1` artifacts;
- keeps replay exact only over observed outcomes and marks unvisited branches as `UNSEEN`;
- routes any useful result back through the existing `CANDIDATE -> VERIFIED | REJECTED | STALE` lifecycle;
- preserves Control Plane, Verification Kernel, Finish Gate, grants, persistence/reconciliation invariants and security policy as non-optimizable authority boundaries;
- identifies Stage 26.4 skill/procedure candidate improvement as the first likely consumer;
- records Dream-RSI (arXiv:2609.14858) as fresh external motivation for history-as-replay.

## Explicit non-goals

- no production code;
- no `ROADMAP.md` or `CURRENT_STATE.md` change;
- no new public tool;
- no EventBus or scheduler;
- no second general planner;
- no widening of `chatgpt-temporary`;
- no production self-modifying loop.

Any concrete implementation remains blocked on fresh repository Stage Research / source-code research.
